<id/12/1248/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Charcoal"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_wood_pulp_fuel/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "charred or burnt wood, which is largely used for fuel on the Continent, and is also valued for making glass, steel, and as a deodorizer when powdered; cylinder charcoal obtained by distilling non-resinous woods is used in the manufacture of gunpowder. *See CARBON. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 95]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated fields — definition use: Auto-match had picked animal (bone) charcoal; the heading is wood charcoal (Canadian exports 1889–97)."@en ;
